                                                        <div class="mb-2">6.1. This Agreement shall commence on the date specified herein (the “Start Date”) and shall continue until the expiration of the contract term and full payment of all amounts due.</div>
                                                        <div class="mb-2">6.2. Either party may terminate the Agreement immediately by notifying the other party if a material breach of any clause of the Agreement occurs, provided that the breach is irremediable or has not been remedied within seven (7) days from the date of notice.</div>
                                                        <div class="mb-2">6.3. The Supplier shall have the right to terminate the Agreement immediately by notifying the Client if the Client declares bankruptcy, fails to pay its debts when due, or has unsatisfactory credit ratings.</div>
                                                        <div class="mb-2">6.4. If the Client terminates this Agreement before its expiration or renewal date without any breach of the Agreement or its annexes, the Client shall pay all fees due for services already provided, in addition to any other costs incurred by the Supplier for the remaining period. In the case of recurring services, if the contract is terminated before the Agreement’s end date, the Client shall pay the fees for services already rendered plus 20% of the fees that were scheduled for the remaining period.</div>
                                                        <div>6.5. The Client (the “Second Party”) shall have the right to terminate the Agreement within forty-five (45) days if dissatisfied with the service, by paying all amounts due without any further obligations.</div>
