                                                        <div>10.1. Each party shall undertake the following: (a) comply with, and continue to comply during the term of this Agreement, with all applicable laws or regulations relating to economic sanctions, trade and export controls, and other restrictive measures imposed, administered, or enforced by any sanctions authority (collectively referred to as “Sanctions”); (b) acknowledge that it is not subject to any actual, alleged, or threatened sanctions proceedings, including litigation, other actions, investigations, inquiries, or enforcement measures (including fines or penalties) by any sanctions authority; (c) acknowledge that it is not, and has never been, listed on any list issued or maintained by a sanctions authority identifying sanctioned persons (the “Sanctions List”); (d) confirm that it is not owned or controlled by any person listed on a Sanctions List, is not resident, domiciled, or located in any sanctioned country or territory, and is not an entity or organization established under the laws of such jurisdictions; (e) maintain, throughout the term of this Agreement, adequate policies and procedures designed to ensure compliance with Sanctions, and implement and enforce such policies and procedures; (f) immediately notify the other party in writing of any actual, suspected, or potential breach of this clause; and (g) have the right to suspend or terminate this Agreement immediately by providing written notice to the other party if the other party becomes subject to Sanctions, is involved in sanctions proceedings, violates Sanctions in any manner, or breaches this clause of the Agreement.</div>
